; Inspect a loaded theory
;
; A loaded theory contributes declarations and labelled facts to the current
; knowledge base. `list` shows what was retained and where it came from.

load natural

; See all retained content whose source is natural.kurt. The short theory name
; and the filename are equivalent here.

list natural
list natural.kurt

; Ask for one kind of content. The category goes before the optional source.

list const natural
list infix natural
list theory natural.kurt

; Without a source, a category covers the whole current knowledge base.

list const

; With no argument, `list` shows the loaded files and their levels. The more
; explicit spelling does the same thing.

list
list files

; Only exported content survives loading. Local declarations, unlabelled
; facts, and intermediate proof lines are absent; inspect the source file when
; you need those lines too.
